<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%# Shown by the service worker (public/pwa/sw.js) when there's no connection. Fully
    self-contained (inline styles, one cached image) so it works offline. %>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#0f0a08">
<title>You're offline — Cultured Africa</title>
<style>
    body { margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: #140d0a; color: #f4ece3; font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; text-align: center; padding: 24px; box-sizing: border-box; }
    img { width: 72px; height: 72px; }
    h1 { color: #fcaa13; font-size: 28px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
    p { color: #d9cbbd; max-width: 340px; margin: 0 auto 24px; line-height: 1.6; }
    button { background: #fb6b10; color: #140d0a; border: 0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 28px; font: bold 16px Georgia, serif; cursor: pointer; }
    button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #fcaa13; outline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <img src="/images/brand/sun.png" alt="">
    <h1>You're offline</h1>
    <p>Cultured Africa needs an internet connection to stream films. Check your Wi-Fi or mobile data, then try again.</p>
    <button type="button" onclick="location.reload()">Try again</button>
</main>
</body>
</html>
